  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because \\mathrm{r}=\\frac{\\Delta}{\\mathrm{s}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{a}^2}{4 \\cdot \\frac{3 \\mathrm{a}}{2}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{2 \\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{12}{2 \\sqrt{3}}=2 \\sqrt{3}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/JR1UpR_Y1fjiniGRhqzwYPJzPpKYnEI3CnWQpKqLPWo.original.fullsize.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned} & \\therefore A=\\mathrm{r} \\sqrt{2}=2 \\sqrt{6} \\\\ & \\text { Area }=\\mathrm{m}=\\mathrm{A}^2=24 \\\\ & \\text { Perimeter }=\\mathrm{n}=4 \\mathrm{~A}=8 \\sqrt{6} \\\\ & \\therefore \\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{n}^2=24+384 \\\\ & =408\\end{aligned}$",
